@startuml replication-overview-p2
title AISafe - Replication and consistency per service (second delivery)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 40
left to right direction

queue "RabbitMQ cluster\n(3 nodes, quorum queues)" as MQ

rectangle "Flight Operations (2 replicas)" as FO {
  component "replica A\n+ PostgreSQL" as FA
  component "replica B\n+ PostgreSQL" as FB
}
rectangle "Airports & Routes (2 replicas)" as AR {
  component "replica A\n+ PostgreSQL" as RA
  component "replica B\n+ PostgreSQL" as RB
}
rectangle "Aircraft (2 replicas)" as AC {
  component "replica A\n+ PostgreSQL" as CA
  component "replica B\n+ PostgreSQL" as CB
}
rectangle "Maintenance (2 replicas)" as MT {
  component "replica A\n+ PostgreSQL" as MA
  component "replica B\n+ PostgreSQL" as MB
}

FA --> MQ : flights.events
MQ --> FB : fo.flights.<replica>
RA --> MQ : airports.events
MQ --> RB : airports.events.<replica>
MQ --> FA : routes (ACL)
CA --> MQ : aircraft.changed
MQ --> CB : aircraft.maintenance / aircraft.flights
MQ --> CA : aircraft.maintenance / aircraft.flights
MA --> MQ : maintenance lifecycle
MQ --> MB : maintenance.aircraft
MQ --> MA : maintenance.aircraft

note right of FB
  Flight Operations: CQRS. Aggregate + outbox in one local transaction;
  events carry the full flight state; idempotent consumers; last-writer-wins
  by revision; deterministic conflict resolution (compensation);
  snapshot from a peer when a replica starts with an empty database. AP.
end note
note right of RB
  Airports & Routes: CQRS (write model + flat read model), transactional
  outbox with publisher confirms, at-least-once delivery, inbox
  (processed_event by eventId UUID), last-writer-wins by lastModified;
  dead-letter queue; reads only from the local read model.
end note
note right of CB
  Aircraft: local JPA state and processed-event idempotency;
  consumes maintenance and flight events and maintains local projections.
  Maintenance: local JPA state, aircraft-reference projection and
  processed-event idempotency; publishes maintenance lifecycle events.
  One database per replica. Legacy HTTP peer/fallback calls remain.
end note
@enduml
